<title>SWEDEN: Skandia says U.S. unit's sales exceed 1995.</title>
<headline>Skandia says U.S. unit's sales exceed 1995.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish insurance company Skandia said on Friday that sales of unit-linked insurance policies of its U.S. subsidiary Skandia Assurance &amp; Financial Services (AFS) reached $2 billion in the first nine months of 1996.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement that sales for the subsidiary totalled $1.6 billion in 1995.</p>
<p>&quot;Growth in the United States is expected to continue,&quot; Jan Carendi, head of AFS, said in the statement.</p>
<p>He said American Skandia now has $7.0 billion under its management.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1003</p>
</text>
